research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.provenance.jsonl-1-{"id":"def-nowhere-dense-meager","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/Analysis/Mathematical_Analysis_%28Zakon%29/06%3A_Differentiation_on_E_and_Other_Normed_Linear_Spaces/6.08%3A_Baire_Categories._More_on_Linear_Maps","https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Meager_set"],"rationale":"Zakon and the Encyclopedia of Mathematics give the closure-interior definition of nowhere dense and the countable-union definition of meager. The local item also fixes residual and the second-category convention, so it is a bundled semantic restatement.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.provenance.jsonl-2-{"id":"def-f-sigma-g-delta","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Borel_set"],"rationale":"The Encyclopedia of Mathematics gives the same countable-union-of-closed and countable-intersection-of-open definitions, with the same ambient-real-line convention.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.provenance.jsonl-3-{"id":"thm-baire-category-r","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Baire_theorem","https://math.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/Analysis/Mathematical_Analysis_%28Zakon%29/06%3A_Differentiation_on_E_and_Other_Normed_Linear_Spaces/6.08%3A_Baire_Categories._More_on_Linear_Maps"],"rationale":"Both sources state Baire category for complete spaces and the dense-open-intersection form. The local statement specializes to the real line, adds the equivalent nonmeagerness clause, and makes the rational-endpoint construction canonical; its proof adapts the standard nested-set argument.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.provenance.jsonl-4-{"id":"cor-q-is-meager-and-not-g-delta","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/Analysis/Mathematical_Analysis_%28Zakon%29/06%3A_Differentiation_on_E_and_Other_Normed_Linear_Spaces/6.08%3A_Baire_Categories._More_on_Linear_Maps/6.8.E%3A_Problems_on_Baire_Categories_and_Linear_Maps","https://math.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/Analysis/Mathematical_Analysis_%28Zakon%29/06%3A_Differentiation_on_E_and_Other_Normed_Linear_Spaces/6.08%3A_Baire_Categories._More_on_Linear_Maps"],"rationale":"Zakon records that the rationals are meager and not G-delta and that a dense G-delta in a complete metric space is residual. The local item packages the complementary F-sigma/G-delta conclusions and supplies its own dependency-local proof.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.provenance.jsonl-5-{"id":"def-measure-zero-and-content-zero","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.mit.edu/classes/18.125/HW2.pdf","https://www.cs.uaf.edu/~maxwell/AY2007/math641/Measure.pdf"],"rationale":"MIT uses the epsilon-small countable interval-cover definition of nullity, while the UAF notes give the countable-cover formulation and the compact finite-subcover reduction. The local term content zero is a deliberately elementary finite-cover convention, so the package is a semantic restatement rather than an exact quotation of Jordan measure.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.provenance.jsonl-6-{"id":"lem-finite-interval-cover-total-length","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://www.cs.uaf.edu/~maxwell/AY2007/math641/Measure.pdf"],"rationale":"The UAF notes state the interval-cover length estimate used in the measure-zero argument and reduce compact interval covers to finite subcovers. The local proof changes the finite-overlap organization but proves the same covering estimate.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.provenance.jsonl-7-{"id":"lem-nondegenerate-interval-is-not-null","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://www.cs.uaf.edu/~maxwell/AY2007/math641/Measure.pdf"],"rationale":"The UAF notes give the countable interval-cover argument showing that an interval of positive length is not null, using compactness to pass to a finite subcover. The local proof follows that argument with this library’s series indexing.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.provenance.jsonl-8-{"id":"lem-countable-sets-are-null","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://math.mit.edu/classes/18.125/HW2.pdf"],"rationale":"MIT Homework 2.1 states exactly that every countable subset of Euclidean space has measure zero. The local proof is the standard geometric-budget cover, adapted to zero-based indexing and the library’s countability convention.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.provenance.jsonl-9-{"id":"thm-countable-union-of-null-is-null","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://math.mit.edu/classes/18.125/HW2.pdf"],"rationale":"MIT Homework 2.1 states exactly that a countable union of measure-zero sets has measure zero. The local proof expands the standard double-indexed epsilon allocation and explicitly records countable choice.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.provenance.jsonl-10-{"id":"lem-content-zero-implies-null","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.mit.edu/classes/18.125/HW2.pdf"],"rationale":"Finite covers are a special case of the countable interval covers in the MIT definition. The implication is a direct local verification from the two definitions; its proof is repository-local.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.provenance.jsonl:11:{"id":"thm-compact-null-is-content-zero","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.mit.edu/classes/18.125/HW2.pdf"],"rationale":"MIT Homework 2.4 states that compact-set measure can be computed with finite covers, semantically the nontrivial direction here. The local statement uses the library’s elementary null/content-zero vocabulary and adapts the open-cover argument.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.provenance.jsonl-12-{"id":"def-cantor-set","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://math.uchicago.edu/~alephnil/notes/MATH-395-notes.pdf"],"rationale":"The Chicago notes define the middle-thirds Cantor set by the same stagewise removal and intersection construction.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.provenance.jsonl-13-{"id":"thm-cantor-set-ternary-description","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.stanford.edu/~ryzhik/STANFORD/STANF205-11/hw205-11-1.pdf","https://math.uchicago.edu/~alephnil/notes/MATH-395-notes.pdf"],"rationale":"The sources identify the Cantor set with ternary expansions using only 0 and 2. The local theorem strengthens the presentation to a uniquely chosen digit sequence and an explicit bijection with binary sequences, and adapts the standard digit proof.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.provenance.jsonl-14-{"id":"thm-cantor-set-properties","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.uchicago.edu/~alephnil/notes/MATH-395-notes.pdf","https://math.stanford.edu/~ryzhik/STANFORD/STANF205-11/hw205-11-1.pdf"],"rationale":"The sources give compactness, perfection, uncountability, nowhere density, total disconnectedness, and nullity of the middle-thirds set. The local item translates total disconnectedness into its available connected-subset vocabulary and proves the bundle locally.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.provenance.jsonl-15-{"id":"def-fat-cantor-set","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.uchicago.edu/~may/REU2021/REUPapers/Jin%2CAlexa.pdf"],"rationale":"The source describes the Smith-Volterra-Cantor construction by deleting successively smaller middle intervals and gives the stage lengths. The local definition encodes the same construction through explicit endpoint and length recursions.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.provenance.jsonl-16-{"id":"thm-fat-cantor-set-has-positive-measure","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.uchicago.edu/~may/REU2021/REUPapers/Jin%2CAlexa.pdf"],"rationale":"The source gives a perfect nowhere-dense fat Cantor set of measure one half. The local statement avoids undeclared outer-measure vocabulary and replaces that value by the equivalent lower bound for every interval cover; the proof adapts the standard removal-length computation.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave8-real-analysis-cantor-continuity.provenance.jsonl-17-{"id":"def-cantor-function","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.stanford.edu/~ryzhik/STANFORD/STANF205-11/hw205-11-1.pdf"],"rationale":"The Stanford source defines the Cantor function by converting ternary digits before the first 1 to binary digits and extending constantly across gaps. The local supremum formula is an equivalent, convention-clean construction.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
